{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Why</b> — the meaning: why should I toil to acquire wealth for the fear of my days of old age, as written: \"until the evil days come,\" and they are the days of old age, for at first he began with \"in your youth.\"" "<b>The iniquity of my heels</b> — joined with \"why should I fear,\" and the meaning: in acquiring wealth, perhaps I will need to seek it by a path that iniquity will lie to me [about]. And the meaning: that I walk in a crooked path, and that iniquity will surround me forever — as if he said, \"why should I fear in evil days, and for the iniquity of my feet surround me.\""], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {1 "The reading יקרנו (with yod) appears in the Hebrew; translated literally as 'will lie to me,' though the syntax is strained and may reflect a textual variant or corruption."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:31:18.585906886Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}